<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Poland, Lithuania and Russia</p><h1 class="st-title">Kuban People's Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1918 CE – 1920 CE · capital Yekaterinodar</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Cossack republic on the Kuban, proclaimed in 1918, that sought union with Ukraine and fought the Bolsheviks while quarrelling with the Whites.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-revolution">Russian Revolution</a> the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kuban-cossack-host">Kuban Cossack Host</a>, descended partly from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/black-sea-cossack-host">Black Sea Cossack Host</a>, set up its own <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuban-rada">Rada</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krasnodar">Yekaterinodar</a>. In January 1918 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/radaa">Rada</a> proclaimed an independent Kuban People's Republic, with a population split between Ukrainian-speaking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossacks</a>, Russian line Cossacks and non-Cossack settlers.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Bolsheviks took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krasnodar">Yekaterinodar</a> in March 1918, and the government retreated with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volunteer-army">Volunteer Army</a>, which recaptured the city in August. The republic had its own ataman, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-filimonov">Alexander Filimonov</a>, and a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuban-rada">Rada</a> in which a Ukrainian-minded faction under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mykola-ryabovol">Mykola Ryabovol</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luka-bych">Luka Bych</a> pushed for federation with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>. This brought conflict with General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anton-denikin">Denikin</a>, who wanted a united <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mykola-ryabovol">Ryabovol</a> was assassinated in 1919, and in November <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anton-denikin">Denikin</a> had the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuban-rada">Rada</a> member <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexei-kulabukhov">Kulabukhov</a> hanged and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/radaa">Rada</a> purged. Demoralised Kuban units deserted, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krasnodar">Yekaterinodar</a> in March 1920, ending the republic.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kuban-peoples-republic.jpg" alt="Kuban People's Republic" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Froztbyte · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Kuban_People%27s_Republic.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1918 CE – 1920 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Yekaterinodar</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Alexander Filimonov, Mykola Ryabovol, Luka Bych</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Eastern Orthodox Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Ukrainian, Russian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/russia">Russia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kuban Republic</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1919&amp;focus=kuban-peoples-republic" aria-label="Kuban People's Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5607 587 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kuban People's Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5927 843L5820 533"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5820 533h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5927 843h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5927 843h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1919&amp;focus=kuban-peoples-republic">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
